# Drupal Application Deployment on Kubernetes

## 1. Project Overview

This project demonstrates deploying a fresh Drupal application on a Kubernetes cluster using a MySQL database with persistent storage.

The deployment uses Kubernetes Deployments, Services, PersistentVolumes, PersistentVolumeClaims, and Secrets to provide a structured environment for the Drupal application.

The objective is to make a fresh Drupal installation available to the Nautilus Application Development team so they can complete the installation themselves.

### Technologies Used

- Kubernetes
- Docker containers
- Drupal 8.6
- MySQL 5.7
- PersistentVolumes (PV)
- PersistentVolumeClaims (PVC)
- Kubernetes Secrets
- ClusterIP and NodePort Services

