## 8. Drupal Database Installation Details

The following database settings were configured in the MySQL Deployment and are available for the Drupal installation wizard.

| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Database type | MySQL |
| Database name | `drupal` |
| Database username | `drupal` |
| Database password | `DrupalDB_2026!` |
| Database host | `drupal-mysql-service` |
| Database port | `3306` |

The Drupal installation wizard can use these settings to connect to the MySQL database.

The Drupal installation itself is intentionally left for the application development team.

**Security note:** The credentials above are demonstration credentials for this lab. In a production environment, use stronger credentials, protect Secret manifests, and avoid committing plaintext credentials to a public repository. The Drupal container also needs the database connection details supplied through its environment or installer configuration.

